Changelog 0.6.0:
  - Fixed the CLI help screen so /VERBOSE is documented correctly as a
    CONFIGURE sub-switch, and shortened its description to keep the option
    table compact and aligned.
  - Added a dedicated CLI_PARSER smoke group covering HELP output, '-' switch
    introducers, '=' value separators, and CONFIGURE with no property.
  - Added DEFAULT_NIC_SELECTION smoke coverage by cloning the core IRQ change
    tests without /ADAPTERNUM and renumbered the downstream test cases to keep
    the suite ordering coherent.
  - Added a COMBINED_TRANSACTIONS smoke group covering the highest-value shared
    CONFIGURE write paths: /IOBASE+/INT, /MODEM+/FULLDUPLEX, /IOBASE+/TR,
    /IOBASE+/BADDRESS+/BSIZE, /OPTIMIZE+/MODEM, and
    /TR:AUTO+/BADDRESS+/BSIZE on Combo adapters.


Changelog 0.5.9:
  - Centralized the release version metadata into VERSION.INC so 3CCFGCLI and
    3CSEED share the same source of truth for their banner/version output.
  - Moved the project changelog out of 3CCFGCLI.ASM into a standalone CHANGES
    file so the assembly source header stays focused on executable metadata.
  - Added explicit /IOBASE boundary coverage for the first and last valid ISA
    addresses (0200h and 03E0h), and renumbered the smoke suite to keep the
    test ordering coherent after the IOBASE block.
  - Fixed the /BADDRESS boundary-state bug caused by conflating the NONE sentinel
    with the minimum valid Boot ROM address.  The valid range remains C0000h-
    DE000h in 2000h steps, while NONE remains a distinct disabled state.
  - Clarified the smoke suite semantics and test-fail behavior in the project
    docs: the authoritative verdict is the assertion log and exit status, not an
    incidental "TEST PASS" marker.


Changelog 0.5.8:
  - Rewrote the help screen (/? /H) for readability.  Each top-level command
    (/? or /H, LIST, CONFIGURE, /VERBOSE) is now separated by a blank line.
    CONFIGURE sub-options are presented as a uniform two-column table with the
    description column aligned at position 39, using the full 80-column width
    with no line overflows.
  - /OPTIMIZE description corrected from "EEPROM optimization target" to
    "Network workload optimization" to accurately reflect its purpose.


Changelog 0.5.7:
  - Implemented /TR (/XCVR alias) CONFIGURE subverb.  Accepts TP, AUI, COAX,
    or AUTO.  Writes EEPROM_ADDR_CFG (word 08h) bits 15:14 (media selection);
    AUTO instead sets bit 7 (auto-select) and clears bits 15:14.  Shares the
    existing word 08h transaction slot with /IOBASE, /BADDRESS, and /BSIZE.
  - Product-ID capability gate: 3C509B-TP accepts TP only; 3C509B-TPC accepts
    TP and COAX; 3C509B-TPO accepts TP and AUI (no AUTO); 3C509B-Combo and
    3C509B-C accept all four values; unrecognised products are rejected.
  - Added CFG_PARSE_TR / CFG_SEEN_TR flags and CFG_ERR_TR_* error codes.
  - Updated CFG_PARSE_HW_MASK to include CFG_PARSE_TR (0400h).


Changelog 0.5.6:
  - Reordered capability gate checks ahead of the "parameter accepted" echo for
    every gated CONFIGURE verb (/PNP, /FULLDUPLEX, /BADDRESS, /BSIZE).
    Previously a request could be echoed as "accepted" and only then rejected
    once the Prepare phase ran its capability check, which read as self-
    contradictory output.  All gate checks now run in a single gate phase
    immediately after adapter selection, before any per-property echo is printed.
  - The Prepare phase for these verbs is now pure staging, since every gate has
    already passed by the time it runs.


Changelog 0.5.5:
  - Added /BADDRESS and /BSIZE CONFIGURE support, sharing EEPROM word 08h with
    /IOBASE. /BADDRESS owns bits 11:8 (Boot ROM base index), /BSIZE owns bits
    13:12 (8/16/32K).
  - Added the same TPO capability gate already used by LIST's Boot ROM decoder.
  - Widened cfg_parse_flags/cfg_seen_flags from byte to word and widened the
    commit mask so a BADDRESS/BSIZE-only change still triggers the shared
    transaction pipeline.
  - Fixed a bug in Cfg_Txn_Read_Current where the inactive-adapter /OPTIMIZE
    path was unreachable dead code.


Changelog 0.5.4:
  - Removed the unsupported LINKBEAT CONFIGURE surface after confirming that the
    original 3Com documentation describes it as a live ASIC register bit instead
    of a confirmed EEPROM field.
  - Added a read-only Link Status line to LIST, sourced from the live media
    status register.


Changelog 0.5.3:
  - Added /OPTIMIZE CONFIGURE support for DOS, WINDOWS, OS/2, and SERVER.
    The CLI stages EEPROM word 0Fh high byte, updates the shared checksum,
    and shows the stored optimization mode in LIST.


Changelog 0.5.2:
  - Added /FULLDUPLEX CONFIGURE support with boolean 0 or 1 input.
  - Fixed /MODEM preparation to preserve bit 15 while updating modem speed.
  - Added PNP capability guard: /PNP now refuses configuration on adapters that
    report no PNP support.


Changelog 0.5.1:
  - Added /MODEM CONFIGURE support with NONE plus numeric validation.


Changelog 0.5.0:
  - Added /PNP CONFIGURE support with boolean 0 or 1 input.
  - Mock state persistence now records the PNP flag consistently with EEPROM.


Changelog 0.4.1:
  - Backend split fully implemented.
  - Real hardware operations are isolated behind backend primitives in
    3CHWIF.ASM; the mock backend in 3CMOCKIF.ASM implements the same contract.
  - Mock backend behavior was aligned to real hardware semantics.


Changelong 0.4.0:
  - Preliminary backend split: real and mock interfaces are separated at compile
    time through the TASM conditional assembly symbols /dREALHW and /dMOCKHW.


Changelog 0.3.5:
  - Adds strict single occurrence validation for every supported CONFIGURE verb.


Changelog 0.3.0 - 0.3.4:
  - CONFIGURE uses one centralized staged transaction facility. /INT and /IOBASE
    handlers only parse and stage requested values, while the shared Cfg_Txn
    facility owns activation, I/O migration, EEPROM writes, checksum update,
    live register synchronization, and verification.


Compatibility note:
  - The original 3CCFG also accepted /PORT as an alias for /IOBASE. This reduced
    3CCFGCLI deliberately omits that alias. Use /IOBASE instead.


Initial Release:
  - The ISA discovery path intentionally follows the behavior recovered from the
    original 3CCFG 3.2 utility.
